ol of Graduate Studies\nFuture students\nHow to apply\nStart your application\nHow to apply\nStep 3: Start your application\nTake control of your future and start your graduate journey now\nStep 1\nSelect your program\nStep 2\nConfirm requirements\nStep 3\nStart your application\nStep 4\nFollow up\nApply now\nBegin by creating your Concordia account (Netname). You can use your Netname to log back into your application if you need more than one session to complete it.\nStart and manage your application\nApplication tips\nHere are some general tips to improve your application experience:\nIf you have a pop-up blocker in your browser, turn it off.\nDon't use the Back button in your browser.\nBe sure to click Save and Exit if you need to leave your application for any reason.\nHave relevant digital files or scanned documents ready to be uploaded.\nHave PDF copies of your transcripts and other supporting documents ready to be uploaded\nHave a valid credit card or debit card available to pay the application fee of $103.00 CAD ($18.91 CAD for Independent graduate students), or $40.00 CAD for a microprogram. The application fee is non-refundable and cannot be waived.\nFor detailed instruction on submitting your graduate application, consult our step-by-step guide.\nNeed help?\nContact the IT Service Desk for technical support at 514-848-2424, ext. 7613 or, email help@concordia.ca.\nDo you have questions regarding admission requirements?\nContact your program assistant\nBack to top\n\u00a9 Concordia University\nSchool of Graduate Studies\nFuture students\nCurrent students\nFunding\nProfessional skills\nPostdocs\nAbout the School\nUseful links\nApply now\nGraduate programs\nThesis-based students\nManage your award\nBook a meeting with us\nGraduate program contacts\nVisit us\nRoom GM-930.01\n1550 De Maisonneuve Blvd. W.\nMontreal, QC H3G 1N2\nGuy-De Maisonneuve (GM) Building\nContact us\n514-848-2424, ext. 3800\nStaff directory\nTerritorial acknowledgement\nConcordia Universit